## browser and returns its number. The browser makes it and answers with
## JSON through `net_deliver`, which runs the callback kept for that number
## inside the same live engine, so no script runs twice. A request the
## browser could not make fails as a network error (TypeError "Failed to
## fetch"; XHR `onerror`).

NET_PRELUDE := r"""
